<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Math functions in grid tracks, gaps and repetitions, in flex bases and gaps, and in transforms and their origins, against definite and indefinite sizes</title>
<style>
  html { background-color: #f6f2ea; font-size: 16px; }
  body { margin: 0; }
  .g { float: left; display: grid; width: 180px; height: 120px; margin: 10px 0 0 10px; background-color: #e0d8c8; }
  .g > div { background-color: #3a7a4a; }
  .g > div:nth-child(2n) { background-color: #2f4f7f; }

  /* Tracks: calc() with a percentage, min(), max(), clamp(), inside
     minmax() and fit-content(), and gaps. */
  .g1 { grid-template-columns: calc(50% - 20px) 1fr; grid-template-rows: min(40px, 50%) max(20%, 30px); gap: calc(5px + 1%); }
  .g2 { grid-template-columns: minmax(calc(10% + 10px), 1fr) clamp(30px, 25%, 50px) 1fr; grid-template(50% + 20px) 0; }
  .t4 > div { margin-left: calc(10% + 4px); transform: translateY(clamp(10px, 100%, 70px)); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
